 Mississippi are beautiful. We started with murder point oysters and ceviche, my DH had the seafood gumbo also. Delicious! For mains, the lamb chops and duck confit. Both were flawless. We ordered the pomme purée and spinach as sides, but honestly the accompaniments to the lamb and duck were plenty. The apple dessert was not too sweet and very good. Amazing!"},{"business_id":"ZoRlLcEsxrzfumd6wHa5Jg","review_id":"ys_LwK0WC88Ybyt-4TsqkA","date":"2022-01-08T22:33:21","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9253925681114197,"text_excerpt":"Chemin a La Mer, could possibly be French for \"Manhattan on the Mississippi\". Donald Link's latest, on the fifth floor of the newly opened Four Seasons Hotel at the foot of Canal Street, is the most upscale, cosmopolitan bar/restaurant in New Orleans. Everything, from the bar to the views, to the food, to the service, to the pricing is very sophisticated and quite stunning. Yes, you'll drop close to a $100 for four drinks or glasses of wine, but it's worth it for a special occasion or to impress out of town guests."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"ZoRlLcEsxrzfumd6wHa5Jg","photo_id":"os47u9mzJi1HZqh7YYYZXw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/os47u9mzJi1HZqh7YYYZXw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9630641937255859},{"business_id":"ZoRlLcEsxrzfumd6wHa5Jg","photo_id":"B_XXuZDq6FOlQuQHfEIzzw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/B_XXuZDq6FOlQuQHfEIzzw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9599665403366089},{"business_id":"ZoRlLcEsxrzfumd6wHa5Jg","photo_id":"DIN5RmFuafd4Q9cWgn7XMw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/DIN5RmFuafd4Q9cWgn7XMw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.912815272808075}]},"notebook_case":null}
